The accepted consequence of D15: an SSL data source whose body has no
colon keyword and no `:=` (a bare call after the header) cannot be proven
SSL and reads as SQL. Expect no edits and no SSL diagnostics, even though
the body is SSL. Recorded so a change to this trade-off is visible.
-- input.ds --
:PARAMETERS sGroup := "ALL";
GetDataSet("SELECT grp_id, grp_name FROM user_group WHERE grp_code = ?", {sGroup})
-- format --
:PARAMETERS sGroup := "ALL";
GetDataSet("SELECT grp_id, grp_name FROM user_group WHERE grp_code = ?", {sGroup})
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
